<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dover, New Hampshire</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dover is a city in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-hampshire">New Hampshire</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, on the Cochecho River near the Piscataqua. Settled from about 1623 as a fishing station, it is the oldest permanent settlement in New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hampshire">Hampshire</a>. It suffered a deadly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abenaki">Abenaki</a> raid in 1689 and later became a textile mill town.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dover-new-hampshire.jpg" alt="Dover, New Hampshire" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MidniteOIL · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dover_City_Hall.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
